## Result

**PASS.** The expanded navigation sheet now follows the measured mobile panel-height cap. At **320×568**, it measures **350px**, leaving **142px of map above it (25% of the viewport)**. The current instruction and primary action remain visible, and the Steps list scrolls internally.

The residual height came from a short-screen override that added 16px above the map’s calculated cap. The shared page layout already measures the visual viewport, header reservation, safe-area inset, and bottom navigation; at 320×568 it sets a **350px** cap. Removing the extra allowance brings the panel back to that limit. The existing calculation is in [studentMobilePanels.ts](src/lib/studentMobilePanels.ts#L6) and is applied from [CampusMapPage.tsx](src/pages/CampusMapPage.tsx#L1683).

## Viewport measurements

“Map above” is the measured space between the top of the panel and the top of the viewport. Expanded measurements were taken with the route’s Steps list open. On tablet and desktop, the existing layout uses a side panel, so map visibility is not represented as space above the panel.

| Viewport | Compact panel / map above | Expanded panel / map above | Steps list: visible / content |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| 320×568 | 282px / 213px | **350px / 142px (25%)** | 31px / 215px |
| 320×720 | 282px / 365px | 464px / 180px (25%) | 145px / 215px |
| 360×640 | 269px / 299px | 404px / 160px (25%) | 85px / 202px |
| 390×844 | 269px / 503px | 557px / 211px (25%) | 144px / 197px |
| 430×932 | 269px / 591px | 623px / 233px (25%) | 210px / 210px |
| 520×738 | 269px / 397px | 478px / 184px (25%) | 170px / 176px |
| 768×1024 | 281px | 675px side panel, 380px wide | 200px / 200px |
| 1024×768 | 275px | 576px side panel, 380px wide | 200px / 200px |
| 1440×900 | 275px | 656px side panel, 460px wide | 184px / 184px |

On mobile, the panel stayed above the bottom navigation with no horizontal overflow. At 320×568, the Steps list had `overflow-y: auto`; its footer gap was 4px, and scrolling moved the list. The instruction measured 32px high, Continue measured 44px, and Exit Building measured 44px.

The prior shared-worktree refinement measured **366px** at 320×568, leaving 126px of map. This change reduced it by another **16px**. Compared with the original 409px height reported in the request, the final panel is 59px shorter.

## Interaction checks

In the CABA-201 → CABA building preview, the stair Continue action switched the visible context from Floor 2 to Ground Floor and advanced to the indoor exit step. The final step exposed **Exit Building**; clicking it displayed the existing arrival presentation. At 320×568, the arrival panel measured 325px, left 167px of map above it, and kept Done and Restart Route at 44px. It did not overlap the bottom navigation.

The panel controls and their callbacks were left unchanged. The focused component tests passed; the browser check covered the stair handoff, final exit, and arrival presentation.

