## A. Root cause

The 350px cap preserved map space, but all navigation controls and the Steps list still shared the same vertical column. At 320×568, that left only about 31px for Steps. Arrival had the opposite problem: a tall centered success card and four buttons exceeded the available content area, clipping the lower actions.

## B. Short-screen layout

On short mobile screens, **Steps** now opens a separate view using the existing `showAllSteps` UI state. It has a Route steps heading, Back to Navigation, an active-step highlight, and an independently scrollable list. The navigation instruction and controls no longer compete with the list; End Navigation stays in the fixed footer.

The Navigation view uses a tighter instruction card and keeps its playback and Steps/Edit controls fully above the footer. The primary action and current instruction remain visible.

## C. Arrival layout

Short-screen Arrival uses a smaller success indicator and less card padding. **Done** and **Restart Route** remain visible; **Previous Step** and **Edit Route** are in a keyboard-accessible More options disclosure. When expanded, the panel scroll area can reveal the extra content without putting the actions behind the mobile navigation.

## D. 320×568 screenshots

Before: clipped Arrival actions.

![Before: Arrival panel at 320×568](verification-artifacts/ui-correction-before-arrival-320x568.png)

After: Navigation view, with the instruction, playback controls, Steps/Edit, and End Navigation visible.

![After: Navigation at 320×568](verification-artifacts/ui-correction-after-navigation-final-320x568.png)

After: separate Steps view, with a 143px list viewport and multiple readable instructions.

![After: Steps at 320×568](verification-artifacts/ui-correction-after-steps-320x568.png)

## E. Responsive measurements

Measured in the rendered Student Map. Mobile “map” is the viewport area above the expanded panel; Steps heights are the list’s usable viewport.

| Viewport | Expanded panel | Steps list | Map above panel |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| 320×568 | 350px | 143px | 142px / 25% |
| 320×720 | 464px | 257px | 180px / 25% |
| 360×640 | 404px | 197px | 160px / 25% |
| 390×844 | 557px | 132px | 211px / 25% |
| 430×932 | 623px | 198px | 233px / 25% |
| 520×738 | 478px | 271px | 184px / 25% |

At 320×568, the list scrolled from 0 to 100px; its content height is 359px. The fixed footer remains outside the list scroller. Mobile bottom navigation stayed 11px below the panel, and no horizontal overflow was measured.

On desktop and tablet widths, the existing side-panel layout remained in use: 380px wide at 768px and 1024px, and 460px wide at 1440px.

Arrival measured 293px closed and 325px with More options expanded at 320×568, leaving 35% and 29% of the viewport above the panel, respectively. All four action buttons measured 44px high. At the other mobile sizes, measured Arrival panels ranged from 293px to 365px; no horizontal overflow or bottom-navigation overlap was found.

## F. Regression and visual verification

**PASS:** The 320×568 Navigation and Steps views were visually inspected in the rendered app. Automated tests confirm the view switch preserves the instruction and camera mode, does not invoke navigation or camera callbacks, and keeps Arrival actions functional.

**PARTIAL:** The Arrival after screenshot, 390×844 screenshot, 1440×900 screenshot, and Light-theme visual inspection were not verified. The preview screenshot tool reported that the browser tab was not drawn because the Freebuff window was covered or minimized. I did not retry capture. Arrival layout and action bounds were measured in the live DOM, but measurements alone do not establish visual acceptance.

## G. Checks

- Focused tests: **102/102 passed** across `RoutePlannerStudentUx` and `studentMobilePanels`.
- Production build: **PASS**. Vite completed; it emitted a large-chunk warning.
- TypeScript: **1,018 diagnostics before and after, delta 0**; neither edited source file had diagnostics. `tsc` still exits 1 because those baseline diagnostics remain.
- `git diff --check`: **PASS**.

## H. Files

Source and regression tests: [UnifiedRoutePlannerDialog.tsx](src/components/map/UnifiedRoutePlannerDialog.tsx#L1135), [RoutePlannerStudentUx.test.tsx](src/components/map/__tests__/RoutePlannerStudentUx.test.tsx#L1428).

Screenshot artifacts: [before Arrival](verification-artifacts/ui-correction-before-arrival-320x568.png), [final Navigation](verification-artifacts/ui-correction-after-navigation-final-320x568.png), and [Steps](verification-artifacts/ui-correction-after-steps-320x568.png). An intermediate Navigation capture also remains at [ui-correction-after-navigation-320x568.png](verification-artifacts/ui-correction-after-navigation-320x568.png).

The two source files already had shared worktree modifications; I preserved them and changed no navigation algorithms, campus data, or backend records.

## I. Readiness

The short-screen Steps and Navigation compositions are visually verified at 320×568, and the Arrival action bounds show no clipped buttons. Overall visual acceptance remains **PARTIAL** until Arrival, 390×844, desktop, and Light-theme screenshots can be captured and inspected.
