# PLV NaviSync audit — **PARTIAL**

The short-screen Arrival clipping is fixed and visually verified at 320×568. The dedicated Steps view is readable and scrolls independently. The full playback and visual acceptance goals remain **PARTIAL**: I live-tested Campus Gate → ICT LAB through its Floor 4 arrival, but did not establish intermediate forward and reverse marker samples across the complete route matrix. Screenshots at 390×844 and desktop could not be captured because the preview renderer reported its window was minimized or covered.

## A. Arrival clipping

The Arrival content exceeded the available short-screen space inside a height-limited, clipped panel. The large success section and four persistent actions competed for that space.

On short screens, the updated layout keeps **Done** and **Restart Route** visible, with **Previous Step** and **Edit Route** in a labeled **More options** disclosure. The disclosure supports Escape and outside-click dismissal; actions close it before invoking their existing callbacks. The success icon and card padding are reduced for the short layout. These changes are in [UnifiedRoutePlannerDialog.tsx](src/components/map/UnifiedRoutePlannerDialog.tsx).

## B. Navigation and Steps views

Compact navigation keeps the current instruction prominent, followed by the primary playback or transition action, Previous/Next, Follow/Explore, and secondary controls.

On short screens, **Steps** opens a dedicated view with a **Route steps** heading, **Back to Navigation**, a highlighted current step, and an independently scrolling list. The fixed End Navigation footer remains outside the scroll area. UI tests confirm opening and closing Steps preserves the step and camera mode without firing route, transition, or inspection callbacks.

## C. Responsive measurements

The following measurements are from the expanded Steps state. Mobile map space is the visible area above the sheet. At tablet and desktop widths, that measure is not comparable because the panel uses the wider layout.

| Viewport | Panel height | Steps list viewport | Map above sheet | Bottom navigation |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
| 320×568 | 350px | 143px | 142px | Footer ends 12px above |
| 320×720 | 350px | 143px | 294px | Footer ends 12px above |
| 360×640 | 404px | 197px | 160px | Footer ends 12px above |
| 390×844 | 557px | 132px | 211px | Footer ends 12px above |
| 430×932 | 623px | 198px | 233px | Footer ends 12px above |
| 520×738 | 478px | 271px | 184px | Footer ends 12px above |
| 768×1024 | 768px | 353px | — | No mobile bottom navigation |
| 1024×768 | 576px | 292px | — | No mobile bottom navigation |
| 1440×900 | 675px | 337px | — | No mobile bottom navigation |

At 320×568, the Steps list has 141px of usable scroll height and 359px of content. Its footer and 44px Back control remain visible. The compact transition state measured 284px high, with 212px of map visible above it. No horizontal overflow was measured at any tested viewport.

At 390×844, DOM measurements showed all four Arrival actions fully inside the panel: each is 44px high, the panel ends at y=768, and mobile navigation begins at y=779. This is measurement evidence only; the screenshot could not be captured.

