## A. Route Preview

Route Preview now opens as one complete, content-sized panel. Its minimized presentation, resize handle, and Expand/Collapse control are removed from preview; normal **Start Navigation**, **Close Preview**, Steps, and route editing remain. Guided Navigation keeps its compact and expanded states.

## B. Use This Route

**Use This Route** now activates the selected route through the existing guarded navigation start flow, so there is no second Start Navigation step. Selecting or highlighting an alternative alone does not start it. The SOS review gate remains in place.

## C. Edit Route pencil

The pencil sits beside the destination in compact and expanded navigation, with an accessible name, tooltip, focus treatment, and a larger mobile touch target. The existing edit workflow is reused.

## D. Guided Navigation dragging

The handle tracks pointer movement continuously, then settles into the supported compact or expanded state using drag distance and release velocity. Pointer cancellation, lost capture, viewport changes, blur, and unmount are handled; reduced motion and keyboard controls remain available. At 320×568, the content area scrolls while the footer stays inside the sheet.

## E. Visual review

The browser bounds review covered all 13 requested viewport sizes. Captures include mobile preview and navigation, a drag in progress, a short mobile screen, and desktop layouts.

