## Changes

The destination labels were being forced into narrow single-line flex slots. Explore Route squeezed the origin and destination together, which could reduce a long name to an unhelpful fragment.

Guided Navigation now wraps long destinations to two lines where space allows. Explore Route shows clearly labeled **From** and **To** endpoints, using the route’s actual location names and wrapping long values within their available width. Compact popovers show the full name on tap, desktop hover, or keyboard focus; Escape and outside clicks dismiss them.

The name and Edit Route pencil remain separate interaction targets. Tapping the name shows details; the 44×44px pencil target calls the existing edit handler. The compact popover placement adapts to Follow and Explore to keep the sheet’s action buttons available.

The mobile Guided Navigation handle strip is 16px high, down from 24px. Its visible grabber is 32×4px, with the 44×44px drag target and existing smooth drag behavior preserved.

