## A. Root cause

The Explore summary placed the origin, generic campus context, map guidance, and a separate Hide Steps button in distinct rows. Those rows and their padding made the summary unnecessarily tall, especially on narrow screens.

## B. Removed and simplified text

“Map context: Campus” is hidden when it adds no useful distinction; meaningful Building/Floor context remains. The visible “Move the map or select a step” helper is removed. Show/Hide is now part of the Steps heading and uses the existing visibility state.

## C. Follow/Explore toggle

The toggle has less internal padding and tighter label spacing while keeping its 44px mobile touch targets and existing mode behavior.

## D. Compact header

The header controls are vertically aligned, with roughly 10px between the controls and divider at mobile widths. The spacing comes from redistributing the existing header space.

## E. Steps and footer

The Steps heading shows the count and an accessible Show/Hide action. On the 320×568 view, the content region can scroll about 90px while End Navigation remains visible.

## F. Responsive results

I reviewed the live preview at 320×568, 360×640, 390×844, 430×932, 520×738, 539×777, 768×1024, 1024×768, and 1440×900.

At 539×777, the summary card is approximately 107px tall, down from about 210px in the earlier screenshot. The full panel is about 551px, down from about 592px. These are approximate screenshot measurements.

## G. Screenshots

