Implemented the panel and Back to campus fixes while preserving the existing route and camera systems.

### Panel states and drag performance

- Arrival now stays expanded and keeps Previous step, Restart Route, Edit Route, and Done accessible. It has no mobile drag handle or collapse control, including when a floor picker had temporarily compacted navigation.
- Plan Your Route remains content-sized and usable; planning and map-pick panels no longer expose misleading resize handles. Guided Navigation and Explore retain their compact, expanded, and draggable states.
- During sheet motion, CampusMapPage now defers repeated overlay measurements and Follow-focus updates until the sheet settles. Drag position still uses the existing animation-frame path; I did not add a second sheet controller or change route playback.

### Back to campus and map visibility

- A mobile **Back to campus** button appears indoors when route controls hide search. It uses the existing guarded `closeFloorPlan` workflow. I verified that it returned to the campus map without closing the planner.
- At 320×568, the button measured 44×44px and the sheet met the tabs exactly: sheet bottom 507px, tab bar top 507px. At 390×844 the labeled button measured 133×44px. There was no horizontal overflow; the mobile control was hidden at 1440×900.
- The attached “Unable to refresh campus map” screen is the published-campus data-loading fallback, shown when the initial campus data request fails before usable data is available. In the current preview the map loaded and the published-version status RPC returned HTTP 200, so the original failure was not reproducible and its specific cause cannot be identified from the screenshot alone.

### Verification and limitations

- The three focused panel suites covered 138 cases: RoutePlannerStudentUx (105), StudentMapControls (26), and studentMobilePanels (7). After updating expectations for the new panel rules and rerunning the affected assertions, all 138 passed.
- One additional active-route context test failed before its assertion because its test renderer remained at “Preparing floor map” (`readonly-floor-plan-scene` was absent; 52 tests skipped). The live Back-to-campus return was verified without an active route; active-route preservation was not verified in that integration test.
- Production build passed: 3,691 modules transformed. Vite reported its existing large-chunk advisory.
- TypeScript still exits with existing repository errors: 512 diagnostic identities, with zero added or removed against the saved baseline in [task-current-typescript.txt](verification-artifacts/task-current-typescript.txt).
- `git diff --check` passed. Live FPS, camera-transition smoothness, and saved screenshots remain unverified: the preview screenshot tool reported that the tab had not been drawn, so I did not retry it.

