## Verdict: PARTIAL

I fixed two confirmed 3D camera defects. I could not verify or claim improved frame pacing: the preview browser was not drawing, and its animation-frame measurement timed out. No renderer or geometry performance changes were made without profiling evidence.

### Camera and focus

- **Stale Room focus:** A Room chosen through search could remain in `searchFocusRef`. The 3D path bypasses the page’s 2D room-focus cleanup, allowing that Room to regain camera focus after a Floor change or Building entry. Manual Building entry and Floor changes now clear the stale focus. Direct Room search still keeps its intended focus.
- **Discovery framing:** Discovery reduced the already calculated Floor-fit distance to 82% or 92%, which could crop the Floor. It now keeps the geometry-derived fit and adapts the elevated camera direction to the Floor’s proportions and visible viewport.
- The existing Follow, Room focus, and route camera paths remain separate. I did not change pathfinding, authored geometry, or emergency policies.

### Performance and browser evidence

**Live rendering, frame pacing, Building switching, and sheet dragging: NOT VERIFIED.** The browser reported that the page had not been drawn; a 61-frame sample exceeded its 10-second limit. Preview logs also contained a WebGL context-lost message, but the undrawn preview prevented identifying its cause. I captured no usable screenshots. The Guest preview exposed the indoor 3D map and Back to Campus control; I did not separately exercise the authenticated Student path.

### Verification

- Focused geometry, camera-pose, and Student Map integration run: **3 test files passed, 109 tests passed**.
- New stale-focus regression: **1 passed; 53 skipped** in the filtered run. Earlier locator attempts failed on duplicate test nodes; the corrected test passed.
- Production build: **passed** with a 2 GB Node heap cap. Vite reported existing large-chunk warnings.
- TypeScript: **still exits with errors**. It reported 1,018 diagnostic identities versus 1,019 in the historical Oct. 26 baseline: 2 new and 3 resolved identities, all unrelated to the files changed here.
- `git diff --check`: **passed**.

### Task-specific changes

I added hunks to [CampusMapPage.tsx](src/pages/CampusMapPage.tsx), [IndoorFloor3DRenderer.tsx](src/components/map/IndoorFloor3DRenderer.tsx), [indoor3dGeometry.test.ts](src/lib/__tests__/indoor3dGeometry.test.ts), and [CampusMapPage.eventOverlayService.test.tsx](src/pages/__tests__/CampusMapPage.eventOverlayService.test.tsx). The shared worktree changes and untracked artifacts were preserved; I did not stage, commit, or deploy.

### Follow-up

The remaining priority is a measured performance run in a visible browser, followed by investigation of the WebGL context-loss event.
