## Result

**PASS:** The Back to campus test fixture is corrected, and the active-route workflow assertions pass. **PARTIAL:** I could not verify live 3D framing or performance because the preview did not produce a WebGL canvas. No performance defect was confirmed, so I made no speculative production-code changes.

## Root cause and route-state checks

The integration test queried `readonly-floor-plan-scene` before its lazy-loaded SVG scene had finished loading. Its mock covered `IndoorFloor3DRenderer`, a different component, so the test saw the “Preparing floor map” Suspense fallback. The test now waits for the scene before exercising Back to campus; its assertions remain intact in [CampusMapPage.eventOverlayService.test.tsx](src/pages/__tests__/CampusMapPage.eventOverlayService.test.tsx#L1679).

The test verifies that Back during Follow preserves the route, destination, instruction, and progress while pausing for inspection; resuming reacquires the indoor route. During Explore, Back preserves the active route and Explore selection; Return to Follow reacquires the route. It also checks that cancelling Edit Route restores the endpoint selections and navigation instruction and progress.

## Performance, camera, and WebGL

- **Performance: NOT VERIFIED.** Frame sampling timed out after 10 seconds, so there are no reliable FPS or frame-pacing measurements.
- **3D framing: NOT VERIFIED live.** The Guest preview showed no canvas after the 3D control was used. I could not visually confirm whole-Floor framing across Buildings, Floors, or viewport sizes.
- **WebGL context loss: UNCONFIRMED cause.** Preview logs reported context loss. Renderer inspection found that React Three Fiber explicitly calls `forceContextLoss()` during unmount, and indoor/outdoor views use separate canvases. That makes the log inconclusive; it does not establish a renderer leak or GPU exhaustion.
- No confirmed bottleneck justified changing camera, renderer, or sheet behavior in this continuation.

## Verification

- Focused regression batch: **9 files, 258 tests passed**.
- Final targeted Back-to-campus integration test: **1 passed, 53 skipped**; the skips were outside the targeted test.
- Production build: **passed**; Vite reported its existing large-chunk warning.
- TypeScript comparison: **1,018 diagnostics at baseline and current; 0 added, 0 resolved**. TypeScript still exits nonzero because of those existing diagnostics.
- `git diff --check`: **passed**.

