I found a concrete ownership defect: camera restoration is stored as one global pose with no context key, and it is passed to both renderers. The indoor floor-fit effect runs before the restore effect, so a stale campus pose can overwrite the correct Floor overview when the indoor renderer mounts. I’m narrowing the fix to make restore requests one-shot and context-scoped, while keeping the existing Follow route camera path separate.
