## Root cause and fix

**The live outdoor camera pose was not directly copied into the indoor renderer on every Building entry.** The renderers are separate, and the indoor overview already fits the selected Floor’s authored bounds to the viewport.

The confirmed leak was a shared, unscoped camera-restore request. Discovery could leave a saved pose—often the outdoor pose—pending, and both the campus and indoor renderers received it. On Floor entry, the geometry fit ran first; the later restore effect could then overwrite that fit. The restore also was not cleared after application.

I changed restore requests to include their owning context: `campus` or the exact `buildingId:floorId`. Only that renderer can receive the pose, and the request is cleared when applied, superseded by a context change, or cancelled by Building entry. Restores are eligible only while the route is idle, preserving route-camera priority for Preview, Follow, Explore, and Arrival. The implementation is in [CampusMapPage.tsx](src/pages/CampusMapPage.tsx#L1023) and the ownership helpers are in [student3dCameraPose.ts](src/lib/student3dCameraPose.ts#L7).

The ordinary Floor fit remains geometry and viewport based; I did not add hardcoded Building coordinates or change its framing algorithm. When the indoor renderer switches Floors or Buildings in place, it now cancels an unfinished focus/recenter tween from the previous context so that it cannot write an obsolete target afterward. See [IndoorFloor3DRenderer.tsx](src/components/map/IndoorFloor3DRenderer.tsx#L1947).

The normal Enter Building handler already cleared searched Room focus. That behavior remains, so a stale search selection does not replace the overview; explicit Room focus and active route camera behavior remain separate.

