## Result

The existing gesture, QR-location, scanner, and feedback work is preserved. I also fixed a 3D touch-gesture mismatch: OrbitControls already mapped one-finger touch to pan, but the shared classifier called it orbit. That could keep Follow in control during a manual pan. Two-finger twists were also treated as no gesture, so they could be mistaken for taps.

The classifier now recognizes one-finger pan and detects two-finger rotation. A pan yields camera control to the user; a twist counts as a gesture and suppresses accidental selection without pausing Follow. Regression coverage is in [student3dInput.test.ts](src/lib/__tests__/student3dInput.test.ts).

## Reused and implemented

- **Map gestures:** Existing 2D controls pan with one finger and pinch around the finger midpoint. Existing 3D OrbitControls handle pan, pinch zoom, and twist rotation. The accessible viewing-angle control changes perspective while retaining the current target.
- **QR location:** The existing campus QR resolver and authored room/entrance data are reused. A scan closes the scanner, marks the resolved location, and fills the planner origin without starting navigation. Room QR locations use the existing room-routing endpoint; building QR locations use an authored entrance or building-level location. Same-campus destination selections are retained, while cross-campus scans clear destinations that cannot belong to the new campus graph. Manual origin changes clear or supersede the QR marker.
- **Location lifecycle:** The temporary marker persists across 2D/3D changes, appears only in its associated indoor context, changes label to “Last scanned location” after 15 minutes, and does not alter route selections when that timer fires.
- **Scanner and feedback:** The scanner has clearer camera errors, a scan frame and beam, flashlight support where available, duplicate-result protection, and camera-track cleanup. Sound defaults off; haptics default on where supported. Preferences are exposed in Student settings and the mobile Guest menu. Arrival feedback uses the shared sound preference.

The new QR page regression verifies that a room QR opens its Floor context, displays the marker, prefills the planner start, leaves the destination editable, and does not start navigation: [CampusMapPage.eventOverlayService.test.tsx](src/pages/__tests__/CampusMapPage.eventOverlayService.test.tsx).

