## Overall verdict: PARTIAL

The angle button is absent, 3D pan/zoom/rotation controls remain, and the compact campus label now displays correctly. Focused tests and the production build pass. I found a live published-graph issue affecting Campus Gate → COED 303: the route goes through Canteen because the graph has no connected outside bypass. The current preview also could not deliver frames for a fresh 3D visual check.

## UI and camera

The shared worktree already contained the angle-button removal and its cleanup. I verified that there is no remaining angle-button wiring, while `OrbitControls` still enables pan, rotation, and zoom in both renderers. Tests also assert the viewing-angle control is absent.

I fixed the campus label case where the live campus name is “MAIN CAMPUS - PLV” but its code is `MAIN`. Mobile now shows “MAIN CAMPUS”; the full name remains the title and accessible label. The campus selector retains a 44px target. The relevant files are [StudentCampusSelector.tsx](src/components/map/StudentCampusSelector.tsx#L109) and [StudentCampusSelector.test.tsx](src/components/map/__tests__/StudentCampusSelector.test.tsx#L70).

The existing Floor-fit system still derives framing from Floor bounds, viewport aspect, and safe space around overlays in [IndoorFloor3DRenderer.tsx](src/components/map/IndoorFloor3DRenderer.tsx#L1911). I made no camera-math changes: saved COED Ground Floor and Floor 6 captures show the whole Floor, but they are prior captures, not fresh acceptance for this change. [Ground Floor capture](verification-artifacts/qa-e2e-coed-entry-exploration-3d.png) · [Floor 6 capture](verification-artifacts/qa-e2e-coed-upper-floor-exploration-3d.png)

The live 390×844 preview rendered 2D. After switching to 3D, the canvas was blank; its WebGL context reported healthy, but a request-animation-frame probe timed out. Earlier logs included repeated context-loss messages during prior hot reloads; none appeared on the latest switch. I could not determine whether those earlier messages were application lifecycle behavior or preview churn. Current 3D framing, Room labels, physical touch gestures, and FPS therefore remain visually unverified.

![Current 390×844 mobile map controls in 2D](verification-artifacts/final-ui-map-controls-390x844-2d.png)

The current screenshot shows four right-side actions: mode switch, recenter, QR scan, and directions. The blank 3D preview capture is retained as [diagnostic evidence](verification-artifacts/final-ui-map-controls-390x844-3d.png).

## Pathfinding findings

I ran the current route planner against the read-only published MAIN CAMPUS graph. The routes are graph calculations; I could not visually inspect their live 3D overlays.

| Route | Result |
|---|---|
| Campus Gate → COED 303, Floor 3 | Standard and Accessible both select Canteen; 518m, 13 instructions |
| COED 303, Floor 3 → Campus Gate | Both select Canteen; 504m |
| Campus Gate → COED 303, Floor 4 | Both select Canteen; 523m, 15 instructions |
| COED 303, Floor 4 → Campus Gate | Both select Canteen; 509m |

The graph’s path enters Canteen at its Primary Entrance, follows the authored 300-unit hallway between its two entrance doors, exits at Entrance 2, then continues to COED. Blocking the five Canteen connector edges disconnects these routes. This points to missing authored outdoor connectivity, not a confirmed route-cost defect. I did not modify route costs or published data. If an outside walkway exists, the Map Builder needs a verified path around Canteen connecting the west and east outdoor approaches; a straight connection would cross the Canteen footprint.

The published data also contains two distinct rooms named “COED 303,” on Floor 3 and Floor 4. The prior route screenshot showed 11 steps; the current graph produces 13 or 15 depending on which room is selected. That discrepancy remains unresolved, and the destination should be clarified or disambiguated in authored data.

A prior live audit covered 18 route cases across 16 pairs, but did not settle this Canteen connection. See the [navigation audit report](verification-artifacts/navigation-edge-audit-20261017/navigation-edge-audit-report.md).

## Verification

- Controls and selector tests: **33 passed** across 2 files.
- Camera, gesture, Floor geometry, route-planner, route-flow, and mobile-panel tests: **207 passed** across 6 files.
- Production build: **passed** with a 4GB Node heap cap. Vite reported the existing large-chunk warning.
- TypeScript: **failed**, with 1,018 diagnostics versus 1,018 in the saved baseline. File/code/message identity comparison found no differences. The `CampusMapPage.tsx` `stairLoading?.label` diagnostic moved four lines after existing code removal; it is the same pre-existing error.
- `git diff --check`: **passed**.
- No FPS or reliable frame-pacing measurements were available. Physical multitouch, camera permission flows, and a fresh live route-playback run were not tested in this pass.

This continuation changed [StudentCampusSelector.tsx](src/components/map/StudentCampusSelector.tsx) and [StudentCampusSelector.test.tsx](src/components/map/__tests__/StudentCampusSelector.test.tsx), and added the two preview screenshots above. Existing shared worktree edits—including the camera, controls, QR, routing, and navigation changes—were preserved. Nothing was staged or committed.

**Readiness:** The UI change is ready for review, but I would not mark the full navigation experience ready for broader Student/Guest acceptance until the COED 303 ambiguity and Canteen bypass are reviewed in the Map Builder, and 3D visuals are checked in a preview that delivers frames.
