## A. Overall verdict: PARTIAL

The panel minimization and state-preservation changes passed focused tests, and Planning and Route Preview were exercised in the live preview. The COED Follow camera improvement is implemented, but I could not visually confirm the result: the preview stopped drawing screenshots and logged repeated WebGL context-loss messages.

## B. Mobile panels

Planning, Route Preview, and Arrival now have an explicit Minimize action and a compact restore pill above the mobile navigation. The dialog stays mounted while minimized, preserving planner inputs, route details, and step-list state. The reducer clears minimization when the route phase changes or the route ends.

Mobile headers without drag handles now have 12px vertical padding, and the Arrival sound control meets the 44×44px touch target. Guided Navigation and Explore keep their existing draggable compact/expanded behavior.

## C. Navigation state

In the live preview, minimizing Planning and restoring it retained the form. The Campus Gate → COED 303 Route Preview kept its route overlay and restored with the same 11 steps. Reducer tests cover preserving Preview and Arrival state and clearing stale minimization on phase changes.

The full Canteen-to-COED navigation was not repeated after these changes, so route progress through those handoffs is not newly verified here.

## D. 3D Follow camera

Follow camera heading now adjusts smoothly as the route bends while preserving camera distance and yielding to manual camera movement. Indoor occlusion checks test whether a wall intersects sight lines to the current route marker or a short distance ahead; only intersecting geometry is faded.

This behavior was **not visually verified** in the browser. The code and focused tests cover the occlusion geometry, but screenshots could not be captured reliably.

## E. Transparency behavior

Door-crossing transparency remains separate from wall occlusion and is driven by route progress. Doors are restored when playback pauses or the route/Floor context changes. No map geometry or route data was changed.

## F. Performance

No FPS or memory measurements were collected. The implementation uses the existing renderer and panel measurement flow; minimizing does not require remounting the map renderer. The preview’s context-loss messages prevent a reliable visual or performance assessment.

## G. Verification

- Focused regression run: **4 files, 258 tests passed**; the follow-up run after the final header and sound-control sizing edits passed **2 files, 114 tests**.
- Production build: passed with a 2GB Node heap cap; Vite reported existing large-chunk warnings.
- TypeScript: **1,018 baseline and 1,018 current diagnostics**. Identity differences were confined to four diagnostics in unchanged `src/services/database.ts`; no new diagnostics appeared in the files changed for this work.
- Live preview: Planning minimize/restore and Route Preview minimize/restore were verified at 574×799. DOM checks confirmed the header spacing and touch target sizing.
- Visual limitations: screenshot capture was blocked, so the COED wall visibility, Arrival presentation, and post-change full navigation remain unverified.

Files changed for this work include [CampusMapPage.tsx](src/pages/CampusMapPage.tsx), [UnifiedRoutePlannerDialog.tsx](src/components/map/UnifiedRoutePlannerDialog.tsx), [ArrivalSoundToggle.tsx](src/components/map/ArrivalSoundToggle.tsx), [IndoorFloor3DRenderer.tsx](src/components/map/IndoorFloor3DRenderer.tsx), [studentRouteFlow.ts](src/lib/studentRouteFlow.ts), [indoor3dGeometry.ts](src/lib/indoor3dGeometry.ts), and [student3dCameraPose.ts](src/lib/student3dCameraPose.ts), plus their focused tests: [RoutePlannerStudentUx.test.tsx](src/components/map/__tests__/RoutePlannerStudentUx.test.tsx), [studentRouteFlow.test.ts](src/lib/__tests__/studentRouteFlow.test.ts), [indoor3dGeometry.test.ts](src/lib/__tests__/indoor3dGeometry.test.ts), and [student3dCameraPose.test.ts](src/lib/__tests__/student3dCameraPose.test.ts).

